{# The button skin as a bare class string, so the <a> in the header, the one
   in the mobile menu, the two in the body and the <button> in the contact
   form wear the same clothes without any of the copies drifting from the
   others. The contrast rule lives here and nowhere else: petrol fill with a
   white label, and a hover that DARKENS – the petrol is a dark brand, so
   lightening would drop the label below AA.

   Emits no markup. Pull it with include(), assign it, hand it to `class`.
   Params: size ('default' or 'compact'). Compact is for buttons that share a
   row with something else – the header bar and the two inline calls in the
   body; it holds 44 pixels so a thumb still finds it on a phone. #}
{%- set size = size|default('default') -%}
{%- set base = 'inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-accent font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-white transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hover' -%}
{%- set measures = size == 'compact'
    ? 'h-11 px-4 text-xs sm:px-5'
    : 'px-6 py-3.5 text-sm' -%}
{{- base ~ ' ' ~ measures -}}
